message: "If you use or discuss this work, please cite it using the metadata below."
title: "Ellipse Perimeter: Ramanujan Approximation and N-Series Geometric Acceleration"
type: article
authors:
  - family-names: Baker
    given-names: C. Wayne
date-released: 2026-10-24
version: v1.2
repository-code: "https://github.com/CWBaker360/ramanujan-ellipse-nseries-comparison"
url: "https://github.com/CWBaker360/ramanujan-ellipse-nseries-comparison"
abstract: >-
  A comparative numerical note contrasting Ramanujan's second ellipse-perimeter
  approximation with two-scale and three-scale polygonal N-Series acceleration.
  Ramanujan is strongest near the circular case, while the tested N-Series
  refinement overtakes it at moderate and high eccentricity.
keywords:
  - Ramanujan
  - ellipse perimeter
  - N-series
  - polygonal approximation
  - Richardson extrapolation
  - eccentricity
  - numerical analysis
